    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439-a2">

                <pb facs="0678" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg566"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Rear-Admiral Davis to
                        the Governor of Jamaica</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Flagship Alabama</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Guantanamo Bay,
                                Cuba</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-01-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It gives me great pleasure to acknowledge
                    your excellency’s letter of the 19th instant, and to assure you of my deep
                    appreciation of the sentiments which it expresses.</p>
                <pb facs="0679" n="567" xml:id="pg567"/>
                <p>I may add without impropriety, I believe, the earnest wish that your own efforts
                    in behalf of your city will be crowned with success and that the work of
                    restoration and rebuilding will progress with rapidity.</p>
                <p>I beg to assure your excellency of the high consideration with which I have the
                    honor to be,</p>
                <p>Your excellency’s obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. H. Davis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
